2026-10-30T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2347) 'Why the game could not be won
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2347) 'Under the repo physics no paddle can win: the teacher never misses.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2347) 'A hit never changes the ball's vertical speed, which stays under 4.1
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2347) 'px a frame. A paddle moves 10 px a frame. Teacher against teacher held
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2347) '0-0 for 30 simulated minutes on three seeds. The classic angle rule,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2347) '`--english 8`, lets the hit point change the vertical speed by up to 8
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2347) 'px a frame. It applies to both paddles, and teacher against teacher
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2347) 'stays even under it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2347) 'What each step fixed
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2347) '1. Simulation first. `sim_right_paddle.py` showed that even a paddle
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2347) '   that is always right loses about 4 points a minute when it holds an
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2347) '   answer for a 4-frame delay. Aiming at the crossing point and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2347) '   stopping there loses almost none, even with 60 percent wrong answers.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2347) '2. Prompt. A two-number prompt at temperature 0 was right 98 percent
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2347) '   of the time on spread cases, but 81 percent on gaps under 30 px,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2347) '   where it answered "stay". The STEPS prompt was right on 80 of 80
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2347) '   close calls at a median of about 105 ms.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2347) '3. Prediction. A mirror-reflection formula tied 2-2. It was wrong on
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2347) '   80 of 80 approaches, because the game pins the ball to the wall.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2347) '   The rollout matched the real hit-test y on 80 of 80.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2347) '4. Staleness. The first 5-minute rollout run led 4-0, then an endpoint
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2347) '   stall froze the paddle for about 30 s and it lost 13 points. A 1 s
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2347) '   request timeout and a 15-frame answer limit fixed it. A planted
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2347) '   endpoint that never answers gave 600 of 600 teacher frames, with
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2347) '   the paddle still moving.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2347  1 LINE
 Text:Written

